  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.1. Increased capacity of member States to formulate and implement a new generation of gender-responsive national employment policies, including for youth</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In September 2021, the Government of Botswana adopted the country&apos;s first National Employment Policy (NEP). The NEP includes a dedicated section on gender and women&apos;s employment, has a strong focus on demand-side policies through private sector development, and lays out a clear short-term action plan to institutionalise its implementation. The ILO provided support towards the development of the Botswana NEP from 2013. The process was long-running, with various challenges and shifts in direction, but ILO technical support (direct drafting support, meeting facilitation, technical advice) has been consistent. The final NEP policy document has been developed by the Ministry of Finance and Economic Development, and the ILO provided to the several drafts and actively participated in various consultative meetings. The ILO&apos;s contribution is explicitly referenced in the NEP&apos;s acknowledgement section.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1.1. Number of member States with new generation of national employment policies addressing country-specific future of work challenges</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
